MeBi (rocq-mebi) is distributed under two licences, by directory.

  Copyright (C) 2024-2026 The University of Kent, David Castro-Perez and
  Jonah Pears.

  THE PLUGIN: GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
  later version (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later; LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt).

    src/                      the plugin: commands, extraction, proof solver
    lib/                      its OCaml libraries (model, terms, utils, ...)
    test/  bench/  scripts/   its tests and tooling
    theories/loader.v         the file that loads the plugin
    and everything else not listed below: build files, documentation.
    (test/ includes the Rocq-level tests, test/rocq/.)

  THE LIBRARY: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your
  option) any later version (SPDX: LGPL-2.1-or-later;
  LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt).

    theories/Bisimilarity.v   weak_sim, weak_bisimilar, mutual_sim
    theories/Premises.v       lemmas the plugin's proofs use
    theories/Transfer.v
    theories/Hiding.v
    theories/Traces.v
    examples/                 the examples, as Rocq developments

Why two. Changes to the plugin itself stay free: that is the GPL. The
library is what other Rocq developments `Require Import`, and the proofs the
plugin generates refer to nothing but `MEBI.Bisimilarity` and
`MEBI.Premises` (and the standard library), both LGPL. So a development that
imports the library, or that contains a proof the plugin generated, is not
itself bound by the GPL; it need only keep the library's own files under the
LGPL. This is the split Rocq makes between itself (LGPL-2.1) and what is
built on it.

The opam package, `rocq-mebi`, carries both: GPL-3.0-or-later AND
LGPL-2.1-or-later.
